# High Tide: "Until end of turn, whenever a player taps an Island for mana, that player adds an additional {U}." A delayed
# triggered ability (CR 603.7b) that is a mana ability (CR 605.1b), so it never goes on the stack but resolves at once with
# the Island's mana ability (CR 605.4a). Turn 3: Bot1's first Island, tapped before High Tide, makes {U} alone; after it
# resolves Bot1's second Island makes {U}{U} with the stack still empty, the additional {U} produced by High Tide, the
# ability's source (CR 106.3, 603.7d), and pays for Lord of Atlantis. "A player ... that player": Bot2 taps its one Island
# in response for {U}{U} - into Bot2's pool, not High Tide's controller's - and casts Counterspell with it. It ends with the
# turn: on turn 4 Bot2's Island makes {U} alone.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
High Tide
Island
Lord of Atlantis
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Counterspell
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#1.Activate
? Bot1.Mana = {U}
Bot1.Hand.High Tide.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#2.Activate
? Delayed = High Tide
? Stack.Count = 0
? Bot1.Mana = {U}{U}
? Bot1.ManaFrom = {U} High Tide; {U} Island
Bot1.Hand.Lord of Atlantis.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
? Stack = Lord of Atlantis
? Bot2.Mana = {U}{U}
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot2.Hand.Counterspell.Cast(Lord of Atlantis)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Delayed.Count = 0
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
? Bot2.Mana = {U}

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Lord of Atlantis; High Tide
Bot2.Graveyard = Counterspell
